concerned because of concurrency of page fault handling:

http://oss.sgi.com/projects/page_fault_performance/

bottomline the fault handling path takes a read semaphore on mmap_sem which means
multiple fault handlers will be in that code simulataneously.
<UPDATE: the read semaphore uses a refcnt to increment reader count. thats no good its no better than a CAS as far
as cacheline ping pong is concerned>

problem comes from the fact that the finest lock they have is per page table. 
thats usually not good enough beyond 4 cpus (heck look whos talking :-))

Solaris avoids this problem entirely by having CAS operations around pte updates
(look at x86pte_update)
